course: dictionary
lesson: 12735
title: Dromaeosaurs: feathered raptors
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dromaeosaur was a kind of small to medium meat-eating dinosaur. It had feathers and a big curved claw on each foot. When you meet a long word, break it into parts and look for clues in the sentence around it.
explain: «The museum had a model of a feathered dromaeosaur with a curved claw on each foot.» Feathered tells you it was covered in feathers, and the claw tells you what its foot looked like. Use the words around the hard word to picture it.
explain: Dromaeosaurs are also called «raptors». So when you see «raptor» in a book or film, it may mean this family of dinosaurs. Velociraptor is one famous dromaeosaur, but the family has many members.
fact: A dromaeosaur is a kind of small to medium meat-eating dinosaur.
fact: Dromaeosaurs had feathers and a big curved claw on each foot.
fact: The dinosaur family Dromaeosauridae is known as «raptors».
fact: Velociraptor is a dromaeosaur, so it belongs to the raptor family.
fact: Dromaeosaurs help scientists show that birds are related to dinosaurs, because both had feathers.
exercise: «The scientist showed us a feathered dromaeosaur.» What is a dromaeosaur? | A fish that lived in rivers | A big bird that cannot fly | *A small to medium meat-eating dinosaur with feathers | A type of tall tree
exercise: Books and films often call dromaeosaurs by what name? | *Raptors | Pterosaurs | Mammoths | Dragons
exercise: «Look at the dromaeosaur claw. It is big and curved.» Find and copy one word that describes the claw. | film | museum | *curved | feather
test: Why do scientists say dromaeosaurs help show that birds are related to dinosaurs? | *Because dromaeosaurs had feathers, like birds | Because dromaeosaurs lived in the sea | Because dromaeosaurs had shells | Because dromaeosaurs could fly over the sea
test: «The raptor in the film had a big curved claw on each foot.» What does raptor mean here? | A type of fish | A large bird of prey | *A dromaeosaur, a kind of meat-eating dinosaur | A ship
exam: What did a dromaeosaur have on each foot? | A flat hoof | Feathers | *A big curved claw | A fin
